.TH SESSLINT-VERIFY 1 "" "SessLint 0.3.0" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-verify \- [read\-only] Verify integrity, hash bindings, and idempotence of a repaired session.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint verify [\-\-source SOURCE_FLAG] [\-\-output OUTPUT_FLAG] \-\-manifest MANIFEST [\-\-plan PLAN] [\-\-json] [\-\-color {auto,always,never}] [\-\-no\-color] [\-\-acknowledge\-side\-effects] [\-\-include\-content] [SOURCE] [REPAIRED]
.SH DESCRIPTION
[read\-only] Verify integrity, hash bindings, and idempotence of a repaired session artifact.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B SOURCE
Path to source session file
.TP
.B REPAIRED
Path to repaired session file
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-source SOURCE_FLAG
.TP
.B \-\-output OUTPUT_FLAG
.TP
.B \-\-manifest MANIFEST
Path to repair manifest JSON file
.TP
.B \-\-plan PLAN
Path to repair plan JSON file (optional)
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output verify verdict as JSON to stdout
.TP
.B \-\-color {auto,always,never}
Control colored output in human report mode Choices: auto, always, never.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color styling
.TP
.B \-\-acknowledge\-side\-effects
Acknowledge tool side\-effects for salvage policy during verify idempotence check
.TP
.B \-\-include\-content
Embed raw transcript content (warning: emits raw sensitive data)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — clean check, or repair executed, validated, and manifested.
.TP
.B 1
Finding / refusal — diagnostic errors found, repair plan blocked, or
execution refused (TOCTOU, SL203).
.TP
.B 2
Operational error — CLI syntax error, file not found, permission denied,
or live-DB path refusal.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-baseline(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-check(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
(docs/SPEC.md, docs/codes/, docs/recipes/, docs/adr/, docs/THREAT_MODEL.md),
or the project site.
.fi

